{
 "id": "reopen-browser-first-key",
 "priority": "P0",
 "title": "After Cmd-Q (Keep) and reopen with a browser page focused, a person's real keys reach the page's address bar (Cmd-L, a typed marker), and Cmd-N then Ctrl-` make a new workspace and terminal; 3 cycles. Cycle 4: the page has a focused text field and the first keys after the reopen are plain keys only; they reach the restored page, in order",
 "why": "reopen-f4 for the lead (STATUS 5612/5646): REOPEN-F4 fixed the terminal case; this is the browser-focused case. Real HID keys after the reopen (CuaDriver), the app's focus model (debug.focus) and the frame. Cycle 4 (lead, STATUS 6493, review of #32207): on the dogfood line a plain key (no Cmd/Ctrl) went to the focused view before the window key hold, so only chords were held; cycles 1-3 start with Cmd-L and could not see it.",
 "source": "REOPEN-F4 (reopen-f4, a02ba201c73876f53)",
